  "summary": "Tom Becker (tom.becker@brightline.example, Finance, user_id 4) asks us to release a scanned-document zip he expects from the copier. Quarantine check shows message Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-09 21:00 UTC, flagged reason MALWARE, releasable=false. Not released: KB-007 and KB-008 forbid releasing malware-flagged mail, and the sender is an external domain not known to us. Needs Tier 2 review: confirm whether docs-share.example is a legitimate copier/scanning service Brightline uses, decide whether the copier should be reconfigured to send to an approved address, and advise Tom. Also noted: quarantine shows a separate spam-flagged message Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, \"Invoice #4471 - October pallets\" (releasable). Not released because the user did not ask for it and has not confirmed it is expected. Account note: Tom's account status is locked with 5 failed logins (password last set 2026-07-23). Not actioned because he did not ask about sign-in; Tier 2 may want to check whether it is related.",
  "reason": "User expects a scan email that is quarantined as malware and cannot be released at Tier 1; a person needs to review the sender and advise the user."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I checked your quarantine and found the scanned document zip from scanner@docs-share.example. Our security filter has flagged it as malware, so I can't release it at the help desk level. I've passed it to our Tier 2 team, who will review the sender and contact you about the next steps. Please don't open the zip attachment in the meantime. If you're expecting scans from the copier, let us know which copier or scanning service sends them, and we'll confirm the right setup. Also, your account is currently showing as locked after several failed sign-in attempts. Please contact us before trying to sign in again, and we can help you get back in.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up user_id 4 (Tom Becker, Finance). Quarantine has two messages. Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, 'Scanned document 0931.zip', reason malware, releasable=false. Not released, per KB-007 and KB-008. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) for sender review and to confirm whether the copier's scan destination is legitimate. Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, 'Invoice #4471 - October pallets', reason spam, releasable=true. Not released because the user did not request it and has not confirmed it is expected. Account is locked with 5 failed logins, sign_in_blocked=false, password last set 2026-07-23. Not actioned because the ticket did not mention sign-in. Tier 2 or the technician should check whether the lockout is related and whether the user needs an unlock.",
